	(text "# MCU SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (MCU BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet BLE_BRIDGE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe MCU subsystem centers on the ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 module (U6) operating from a regulated +3.3V digital supply rail. It controls system status\nindication LEDs, SPI/I2C communication, LoRa transceiver interfacing, USB-UART debugging, expansion header routing, and external window watchdog\nsupervision.\n\n1. SYSTEM CORE AND POWER\n• Core Module: U6 (ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8).\n• Power Rail Filtering: Parallel ceramic decoupling capacitors C14 (200 nF), C15 (100 nF), C16 (100 nF), and C17 (10 uF) connected directly across\n  +3.3V (Pin 2) to GND (Pins 1, 40, EP).\n• Hardware Reset: Active-LOW RESET_CHIP line on EN (Pin 3) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R27 (10 kohm) and debounced by C18 (100 nF) via SW1 push\n  button. Driven by watchdog supervisor U7 output (~RESET).\n• Hardware Watchdog Supervisor: U7 (TPS3851H33EDRBR) monitors system software execution via RST_WDI (IO21 / Pin 23). If no heartbeat pulse is\n  toggled within the 323.4 ms window (C45 100 nF), U7 asserts ~RESET_CHIP LOW to perform a hard chip reset.\n• Sleep Mode Watchdog Disable: WCD_SLEEP (IO48 / Pin 25) drives U7 SET1 (Pin 5). Driving IO48 LOW before entering deep sleep cleanly disables the\n  watchdog supervisor.\n\n2. BOOT, STRAPPING AND MEMORY CONFIGURATION\n• Bootloader Download Mode: IO0 (Pin 27) connected to BOOT0 net, pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R28 (10 kohm) and grounded via SW2 push button (debounced\n  by C19 100 nF).\n• Octal PSRAM Protection: IO35 (Pin 20), IO36 (Pin 29), and IO37 (Pin 30) explicitly unassigned (NC) to avoid memory bus conflicts with internal\n  Octal PSRAM routing.\n• ROM Log Suppression Strapping: IO45 (Pin 26) and IO46 (Pin 16) pulled LOW to GND via R25 (10 kohm) and R26 (10 kohm) respectively to suppress\n  internal ROM boot debug messages.\n\n3. STATUS LEDS & INTERFACE LOGIC\n• BATT_ALERT Indicator: Active-LOW LED D3 (LOW) driven by BATT_ALERT net (IO48 / Pin 25), pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R24 (1 kohm).\n• LED Scanning: Driven by IO38 (Pin 31) through current-limiting resistor R20 (1 kohm) to GND (D4 SCAN).\n• LED Connected: Driven by IO39 (Pin 32) through current-limiting resistor R21 (1 kohm) to GND (D5 CONNECTED).\n• LED Heartbeat: Driven by IO40 (Pin 33) through current-limiting resistor R22 (1 kohm) to GND (D6 HEARTBEAT).\n• LED ON: Driven by IO41 (Pin 34) through current-limiting resistor R23 (1 kohm) to GND (D7 ON).\n\n4. MASTER GPIO ASSIGNMENT TABLE (REV 2.3 EXACT SCHEMATIC MATCH)\n• GND: System ground reference connection\n• +3.3V: Main +3.3V system power supply rail\n• EN: RESET_CHIP - System hardware reset line (Pulled HIGH via R27 10 kohm, connected to U7 ~RESET)\n• IO0: BOOT0 - Bootloader download mode select (Pulled HIGH via R28 10 kohm, debounced by SW2/C19)\n• IO1: SPI.SPI_NSS - LoRa Transceiver Chip Select line\n• IO2: NC - Unassigned / Spare GPIO\n• IO3: USB_DATA_USB_D- - Native USB 2.0 Full-Speed Data Minus line\n• IO4: USB_DATA_USB_D+ - Native USB 2.0 Full-Speed Data Plus line\n• IO7: RESET_LoRa - Active-LOW hardware reset line for SX1262 LoRa transceiver\n• IO8: I2C_BUS.SCL - Shared I2C bus clock line (Pulled HIGH via R17 4.7 kohm)\n• IO9: I2C_BUS.SDA - Shared I2C bus data line (Pulled HIGH via R18 4.7 kohm)\n• IO10: BUSY_LoRa - SX1262 LoRa internal status indicator line\n• IO11: DIO1 - SX1262 LoRa interrupt request line\n• IO12: SPI.SPI_MISO - Shared SPI bus Master-In Slave-Out data line\n• IO13: SPI.SPI_MOSI - Shared SPI bus Master-Out Slave-In data line\n• IO14: SPI.SPI_SCK - Shared SPI bus serial clock line\n• IO21: RST_WDI - TPS3851H33 Watchdog WDI input pulse line (Toggled during execution)\n• IO35: NC - Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect)\n• IO36: NC - Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect)\n• IO37: NC - Reserved for internal Octal PSRAM (Unconnected / No Connect)\n• IO38: LED Scanning - Status LED drive line for D4 SCAN (1 kohm R20)\n• IO39: LED Connected - Status LED drive line for D5 CONNECTED (1 kohm R21)\n• IO40: LED Heartbeat - Status LED drive line for D6 HEARTBEAT (1 kohm R22)\n• IO41: LED ON - Power indicator LED drive line for D7 ON (1 kohm R23)\n• IO42: NC - Unassigned / Spare GPIO\n• IO45: GND (Strapping) - Boot strapping pin (Pulled LOW to GND via R25 10 kohm)\n• IO46: GND (Strapping) - Boot strapping pin (Pulled LOW to GND via R26 10 kohm)\n• IO47: BATT_ALERT - Fuel gauge state-of-charge interrupt input (Drives D3 LOW)\n• IO48: WCD_SLEEP - Watchdog enable control line (U7 SET1 pin, Pulled LOW via R31 100k ohm)\n• TXD0: UART_TX - Debug hardware UART0 transmit line\n• RXD0: UART_RX - Debug hardware UART0 receive line\n\n5. EXPANSION HEADER J3 INTERFACE\n• Pin 1: I2C_BUS.SCL (Shared I2C clock line from IO8 / Pin 12)\n• Pin 2: I2C_BUS.SDA (Shared I2C data line from IO9 / Pin 17)\n• Pin 3: SPI.SPI_MOSI (Shared SPI Master-Out Slave-In from IO13 / Pin 21)\n• Pin 4: SPI.SPI_SCK (Shared SPI clock from IO14 / Pin 22)\n• Pin 5: SPI.SPI_MISO (Shared SPI Master-In Slave-Out from IO12 / Pin 20)\n• Pin 6: GND (Ground reference connection)\n• Pin 7: +3.3V (Digital system 3.3V supply)\n• Pin 8: UART_RX (Hardware UART0 receive on RXD0 / Pin 36)\n• Pin 9: +3.3V (Digital system 3.3V supply)\n• Pin 10: UART_TX (Hardware UART0 transmit on TXD0 / Pin 37)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
